---
import HABase from '../../layouts/HABase.astro';
import { blueprints, shortBlurb } from '../../lib/blueprints';
---
<HABase title="Showcase — 1:1 HA config replica" active="showcase" crumbs="Showcase · interactive HA editor replica" heading="Showcase">
  <p class="section-sub" style="max-width: 720px;">
    Every blueprint below renders the same sections, fields, defaults and selector types as Home
    Assistant's blueprint editor — entity pickers, sliders, toggles, duration, colour lists and all.
    Configure with mock entities, watch the automation YAML update live, then import for real.
  </p>
  <div class="ha-grid2">
    {blueprints.map((b) => (
      <div class="ha-card bp-card">
        <div><span class="pill blue">{b.sections.length} sections</span> <span class="pill">{b.fieldCount} inputs</span></div>
        <h3>{b.name}</h3>
        <p>{shortBlurb[b.slug] ?? ''}</p>
        <div class="row">
          <a class="ha-btn" href={`/showcase/${b.slug}`}>Open replica</a>
          <a class="ha-btn ghost" href={`/docs/${b.slug}`}>Docs</a>
        </div>
        <div class="small muted">{b.sections.map((s) => s.name).join(' · ')}</div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="ha-card" style="margin-top: 16px;">
    <b>How fidelity is guaranteed</b>
    <p class="small muted">
      <code class="inline">bun run data:build</code> parses <code class="inline">blueprints/*.yaml</code> into
      sections → fields → selectors (entity, number, text, boolean, duration, select, condition, action,
      color_rgb, color_temp, object). The React editor renders each selector the way HA does.
      Collapsed sections default exactly as the YAML declares. If the YAML changes, the showcase changes.
    </p>
  </div>
</HABase>
